ers there is never I think  being a moment when the richer ship  hasn't been really deep and strong but  also never a moment where there hasn't  been one or two issues on which we  disagree two more things that you  mentioned terrorism dealing with  terrorist attacks five attacks in 2017  in the UK mi5 saying they're running  approximately 500 operations looking at  3,000 subjects of interest radical Islam  is still a major concern for the UK as  it is for the u.s. mi5 do an  extraordinary job in combating radical  Islamic terrorism in pre-empting  terrorist crimes before they happen but  the threat is ever-present is going to  be there for a generation and we will be  intensify efforts tackle it and working  with our partners in beauty of course  here in Washington to take this on  finally you mentioned brexit and there  is still a lot of angst about how this  is all gonna work I know in the UK  obviously figuring it out but in the  world economy and how it's going to  affect things where do you put it now  and and the prospects of a brexit the  next task is to agree transitional  arrangements that will give certainty  and continuity not just a British but  two international businesses present in  the UK and beyond that we need to work  out a future trading relationship with  the EU  I'm confident we will achieve all of  that but also confident we have this  great opportunity then to forge much  stronger trade relationships with the  rest of the world free trade agreements  starting with here in the US and you  sense that the economy is on the upswing  Dubai is is doing fine I have to say I'm  a bit envious of quite how strongly the  US economy has performed over the last  year or two but we are growing solidly  and steadily mr. ambassador we  appreciate the time thank you very much  for giving the opportunity
 

